    {
      "id": "claim_8a4d4e9ce1e04020aea13e83ce8ac34f",
      "statement": "service_search answers with a signed service_quote whose payload echoes the query, reports available as bool(matched), returns the matched catalog subset by bidirectional lowercased substring matching (empty services matches everything; a 'corte' query also matches 'corte+barba'), echoes the full marketplace_policy dict, and is audited as marketplace.search; availability is catalog presence, not live calendar state, and the requested date is echoed but not used.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/client.py#L238-L252",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd33463e6c50c140c6136ded8318cedf58dbd578a30bec0ecc943610c2a62e32:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L352-L369",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:55fb4651e7789e7b8a03313d26526cce75a60176c40f8d5fdcbcfae1cd904af8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_marketplace.py#L45-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24a1ce1ff407adadc59de4e446706330569ef65f3aead774d4860e0f4e3de6ba:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0b0c3e799bb54f70adb09df8d6506d7e",
      "statement": "Every inbound marketplace message first passes _check_marketplace_sender, which rejects a directory-blocked sender fingerprint with PERMISSION_DENIED before consuming any token, then charges the sender from a dedicated stricter rate-limit catalog: a marketplace bucket with capacity 10 and refill 0.05/s plus a per-sender global bucket with capacity 20 and refill 0.1/s, both consumed on each message via RateLimiter.check (which raises transient RATE_LIMITED with a retry_after hint when either is empty).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/rate_limiter.py#L109-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:60a8cd863187af658856f65e3a643a87a94665528efd043d20a6b60ed851de49:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L337-L350",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0db5512ed44780d2d5691ee96195ac8ef0dd448d89506222a7227ab2fcb0d664:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_marketplace.py#L85-L98",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:12d9d6404ac6c075a876ed1caecd8d82a716929880ac240cf6f269ea5f7b4611:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1fd1c425cba149b28123a412de3beb5d",
      "statement": "Blocking is the instant kill switch for marketplace traffic: Directory.block creates or flips a blocked tombstone and empties the record's permission matrix even for a fingerprint never seen as a friend, and because bootstrap verification works for unknown senders, a blocked stranger is still identity-verified and then refused with PERMISSION_DENIED rather than left indistinguishable from an impostor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/directory.py#L295-L310",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:de343e29888e4a2dba84325de26ca51f5a15492d98d713c54dff2f4a27e47979:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L337-L350",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0db5512ed44780d2d5691ee96195ac8ef0dd448d89506222a7227ab2fcb0d664:"
