          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:73bbe3dbec2f3246731556a3142a1a71b1b852b9cb44d874797407c86ded9cb8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2b476740d0de476ca004d57fca708b92",
      "statement": "The client marketplace helpers are stateless outbound calls that bypass the alliance machinery: service_search and service_book sign envelopes embedding the sender's public key and POST them directly to business_endpoint + '/haap/messages', never consulting the local directory, the outbound permission guard, or the client rate limiter (unlike delegate_task through _send), and they record no task or friend state locally; error replies are normalized into raised exceptions via error_from_code, service_book audits client.marketplace.booked on success and client.marketplace.book.error on failure, and service_search leaves no client-side audit event.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/client.py#L237-L273",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:490020bd0586fc990842e752246ce7a0161db8d1657a4971a79f7193a86f195f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/client.py#L95-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6dc2dd18304970b40045ea0e1a30741244cf8b6e51cf43ecbc0252aa295df72c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5ad3701aed6342a495b9fa1190fe6f1f",
      "statement": "service_cancel exists at the protocol and server level but is incomplete as a backend operation: _on_service_cancel runs the shared sender checks, audits marketplace.cancel with the booking id truncated to 40 characters, and replies a completed task_result with detail cancelled true, but it neither creates a task nor calls on_task, and HAAPClient exposes no service_cancel helper in this revision.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/client.py#L237-L273",
